    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nCurrently, if you have a buffer like\n```\nline1\nline2\nline3\n```\nAnd you place a cursor on the first two lines with\n```\nQjQj\n```\nThen you have two multicursors, and one normal cursor. But if you do `[C`, the cursor on the last line disappears.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe main cursor would be treated more like a multicursor, and so when we left the current position, a cursor would be left behind.\n\nPerhaps the main cursor actually _should_ be a multicursor, and when reading from the nvim.multicursor namespace, it would be included with some data (`{ primary = true }`). This would mean the namespace would never be empty, but you could still gate on multiple cursors by checking if the returned table has length `> 1`. For plugins that do multicursor stuff, this might make behavior more intuitive.\n\nThat's not necessary, for the record, and could be moved to a separate issue. Just thinking out loud.",
