            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> don't know how to make sense of that, since every motion \"leaves the current position\".\n\nI mean \"leave\" as in \"deposit\" - place a multicursor where we just left our main cursor. `QjQj` only places two multicursors, and so when you use `[C`, the third line has no cursor on it anymore. But I would expect my primary cursor to just be \"one of the cursors\", rather than needing _another_ `Q` to be run before I leave.",
