        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> and so when you use `[C`, the third line has no cursor on it anymore.\n\nbut you didn't hit `Q` there... if you do, then everything will work. it won't \"double\" the operations; if the primary cursor overlaps a cursor, it counts as 1 total cursor.\n\nthat's a very obvious model for users to understand. whereas, i'm not really sure how it would be obvious which motions \"deposit\" a cursor behind them. that seems confusing...",
