        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I think the point is that for multicursor users \"go to next cursor\" is interpreted as/a less desirable command than \"make the next cursor the primary one\", i.e. they expect/want \"go to next cursor\" to not \"decrease\" the amount of cursors, ever.\nOtherwise `[C` decreases the amount of cursor on the first time, but not on the second input, i.e. it acts 'differently' on repeat inputs,\nwhich is confusing.",
